{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"7ffe49cc271567855b727139bf2f4a0a980ccc3e36fcd75ef7d5df10c55b06ad","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion verifier and close gate","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/completion.py","src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reconcile_verdict","deterministic_child_failure","COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE","result['remediation']","_render_verdict_text"],"problem_keywords":["completion verifier","FAIL verdict","remediation guidance","ticket comments","evidence channel","discoverability"],"propositions":["When completion verifier returns FAIL, callers lack guidance on documenting supporting evidence as ticket comments, causing them to pursue wrong escape hatches instead of the intended evidence channel.","FAIL verdicts must carry a generic, stable remediation guidance string that instructs callers to record evidence (paths, commands, outputs, reasoning) as ticket comments and explains the verifier reads comments on re-verification.","The remediation guidance must be set at a single chokepoint (reconcile_verdict) and applied to both agentic FAIL and deterministic child-closure FAIL verdicts.","Blocked close and verify-completion text output must surface the remediation guidance to the caller whenever a FAIL verdict is displayed.","The remediation guidance text must be generic, name the ticket comments channel explicitly, and must not mention forcing closure."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818250034723262,"uuid":"e7528e90-9ee0-46f4-808c-3d03ea3dcd68"}